WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.136
The President lied
about his poll numbers

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.237
after a speech in Iowa
where farmers are hurting

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.639
from his trade policies.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.941
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:13.279
♪♪

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.915
Iowa's an awkward place
for Trump to be right now

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.117
because there are
a lot of farmers there

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.019
who have been hurt
by his trade war with China,

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.822
although, really, anyplace
is an awkward place to be

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.690
for Trump just in general.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.393
He's the only person
I've ever seen

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.028
who looks out of place,
every place.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.663
I mean, he never
looks comfortable

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.964
no matter where he is.

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:33.666
He's always drenched in sweat.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.501
His tie is always
down to his junk.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.469
And even when he's
at the White House,

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:40.273
surrounded by microphones,
he stands with his chest

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:45.578
puffed out like a penguin
trying to scare away a predator.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:50.216
I mean, if that wasn't on CNN,

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.585
you'd think it was
Animal Planet.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.054
"And if you take a look
at this little fellow,

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.790
he senses his nest
is being threatened...

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.493
and puffs out his chest
all the while using

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:06.132
his ample backside
to protect his precious eggs."

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.935
Trump's trade war...

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.637
Trump's trade war comes
after he spent years

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:14.607
as a candidate and president
courting farmers in the Midwest.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.041
For example,
during the campaign,

00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:18.111
Trump couldn't be bothered
to actually come up with

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.880
a specific plan to help farmers
or Midwestern states,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.249
so instead he just claimed
he loved Iowa so much,

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.684
he might just buy a farm
and move there.

00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:28.954
-Iowa, we love you.
We thank you.

00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:32.592
You're special. We will be back
many, many times.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.628
In fact, I think I might
come here and buy a farm.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.763
I love it. Okay?

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.299
Iowa! I love Iowa.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.500
We've really hit a note
with evangelicals.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.402
We've hit a note
with the Tea Party

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:45.237
and with just
the people of Iowa.

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:46.806
I'm all over the place.
I like it! I love it!

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.041
Maybe I'll just buy --
I think I'm going to buy a farm

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:51.010
and settle down over here.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.012
Right? No, I think I will.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.181
A medium-sized farm

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.317
'cause I don't know
if I want to work that hard.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.818
Right?

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:01.453
-All right. First of all, I
can't imagine Trump as a farmer.

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:05.091
They'd have to put
tractor wheels on his golf cart.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.860
I mean,
the closest he's ever come

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:12.332
is the farmer's tan
he has under his eyes.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:15.134
But, also, I do need to ask

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.336
what is going on
with this voice here?

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:19.938
With just the people of Iowa,
I'm all over the place.

00:02:19.938 --> 00:02:21.707
I like it! I love it!

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:24.543
-He's like --
Sounds like Gilbert Gottfried

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:28.280
after inhaling helium
and sitting on his own balls.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.449
And, seriously, how did we
end up with a president

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:32.417
who sounds like Jar Jar Binks?

00:02:32.417 --> 00:02:33.786
-I like it! I love it!

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.688
-Oh, mui mui! I love you!

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.723
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:40.226
-I mean...

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:43.396
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:46.365
But Trump -- Trump can't
even talk in a coherent way

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:48.968
about legitimate issues
that really do matter

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.037
to farmers and people
in rural areas,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.538
like expanding broadband access.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.840
Trump tried to discuss it
in his speech last night,

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.976
and it was so hard to follow
what he was saying

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:59.612
that even Fox Business network
cut away.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:05.084
-We secured nearly $1.2 billion
to expand rural broadband.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:10.189
Which you need very badly.
You need very badly.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:13.626
They have not treated the
Midwest well with broadband,

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.129
with anything having to do
with the word "computer."

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:18.064
I look at some
of those tractors,

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.699
and they don't even hook up.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.834
They're all set, but you don't

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.369
have the capability here
in terms of --

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.471
-All right.
We're gonna talk with our panel

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.773
about a lot of what
the President's been saying.

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:29.976
He's offering a lot of fodder
for discussion.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:34.947
-I mean, that was the TV version
of rolling up your car window.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.983
"Oh, man, this guy
is really rambling.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:40.086
Yes. No! No squeegee!
Thank you!

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.887
No. Goodbye!

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:45.391
Thank you. Goodbye!"

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.527
The thing that's so weird
about Trump

00:03:48.527 --> 00:03:51.597
is you can tell there are bits
and pieces of real information

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.633
there that he half-remembers
from a briefing.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.467
He wasn't really paying
attention to it.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.036
Then when he tries
to describe it,

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:59.204
he's only capable of
spitting out a few key words,

00:03:59.204 --> 00:04:01.240
like when Trump said this.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.642
-I look at some
of those tractors,

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.043
and they don't even hook up.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:08.414
-I mean, that came
from something real.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:11.083
But he talks about it
like tractors literally have

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:15.521
a giant hole for a plug
labeled "Internet Hook-Up."

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.890
So, now Trump's trade policies
are hurting him

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.059
in Midwestern states
that he won in 2016.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.195
In fact, Trump's poll numbers
in key states

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.297
are apparently so bad,
he's told his aides

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.998
to straight-up pretend
they don't exist.

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:28.367
"The New York Times" reported
that after being briefed

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:29.668
on a devastating 17-state poll

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:31.337
conducted by
his campaign pollster,

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.873
Trump told aides to deny
that his internal polling

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.409
showed him trailing Joe Biden
in many of the states
he needs to win.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:38.777
I wouldn't be surprised if they
were making up new states

00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:40.279
just to cheer him up.

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:42.214
"Good news, Mr. President.
You're winning big

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:46.152
in Old Jersey, East Dakota,
Californication, and Blorf."

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.788
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.923
Today during a meeting
in the Oval Office,

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.126
Trump doubled down
on his lie about polling,

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.361
but it was especially gross
because he did it

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.630
during a meeting
with the president of Poland

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.031
where there's growing concern

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.066
over the decline
of democratic institutions.

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:03.002
After Trump attacked polls
and the media,

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.804
he and the Polish president were
both asked about those concerns

00:05:05.804 --> 00:05:07.239
and shrugged them off,

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:09.641
although Trump didn't really
seem to know much about it.

00:05:09.641 --> 00:05:11.177
-There were fake polls

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.746
that were either put out
by the corrupt media,

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:17.516
because much of the media
in this country unfortunately
is corrupt.

00:05:17.516 --> 00:05:19.719
I have to tell you that,
Mr. President.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.992 line:0%
I'm not concerned.
I know the president very well.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.627 line:0%
I know the people and the
leadership of Poland very well.

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:31.731 line:0%
I'm not concerned at all.
But you may want to say
something about that.

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:44.376 line:0%
-That's what I hear.

00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:47.012
-Oh.

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:49.648
Oh, that's what you hear?

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:52.952
Do you mean
that's what you just heard?

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:54.553
He just lets other people talk

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:56.355
and then chimes in
when he agrees.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:59.091
He's the Ed McMahon
of presidents.

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:01.093
Of course, it's early --

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:03.730
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:08.066
Well, Sal, I think you'll agree,
I was right on that one.

00:06:08.066 --> 00:06:12.237
I went to the mat for that joke,
and I think we'll agree

00:06:12.237 --> 00:06:14.073
I was right and you were wrong!

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.508
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:18.744
It was so funny,
they forgot to make any noise.

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:22.815
They laughed so hard,
it went in backwards.

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:25.284
[ Gasps ]

00:06:28.153 --> 00:06:30.690
Right you are, sir!

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.659
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:34.860
Oh, good.

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.796
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.864 --> 00:06:40.733
[ Laughs ]

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:43.202
Of course it's early, and we
should be skeptical that Trump's

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.803
loyal base will suddenly
desert him,

00:06:44.803 --> 00:06:47.673
but there have at least been a
few anecdotal reports of voters

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:50.442
in the Midwest who back Trump
having second thoughts,

00:06:50.442 --> 00:06:53.412
as one Ohio farmer explained
in an interview with CNN.

00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:55.881
-We're in a free fall out here
in agriculture.

00:06:55.881 --> 00:06:57.416
Those tariff dollars

00:06:57.416 --> 00:07:00.352
come directly
from American importers,

00:07:00.352 --> 00:07:03.555
from American companies
that hire American workers

00:07:03.555 --> 00:07:05.424
that pay American taxes,

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:06.892
and then they turn around

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:10.863
and push that out
to consumers to pay.

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:15.367
And why the farming community
has to take one in the shorts

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:18.904
just so that the President
can have a talking point

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:23.475
and be tough on China
just is a little bit beyond me.

00:07:23.475 --> 00:07:25.511
-Wow. You know Trump
would hate to hear that.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:27.580
Although, I bet his staff
goes through his DVR

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:30.315
and dubs over any negative
news coverage of him.

00:07:30.315 --> 00:07:32.451
-Pres Trump:
I like it! I love it!

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:34.386
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.756
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:42.194
Also, it should be noted
that farmer laid out a clearer

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:43.695
and more articulate explanation

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:46.165
of how tariffs work
and why they're hurting farmers

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.434
than the President of the United
States ever has in his life.

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:51.169
In fact, compare that
answer to what Trump said
about his China tariffs

00:07:51.169 --> 00:07:54.073
during a meandering phone
interview with CNBC on Monday.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:55.574
We'll even add subtitles

00:07:55.574 --> 00:07:57.710
so you can try to follow
what he's saying.

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:46.425
-What are you talking about?

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:49.294
How did you go
from China to senators

00:08:49.294 --> 00:08:50.595
to India to French wine?

00:08:50.595 --> 00:08:52.631
Did you drink some French wine?

00:08:52.631 --> 00:08:54.400
You're rambling
like a tourist in Napa

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.601
who didn't realize
that after you taste the wine,

00:08:56.601 --> 00:08:58.170
you're supposed to spit it out.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.339
I mean, is that why
you're standing like

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:03.275
you're about to fall
flat on your face?

00:09:03.275 --> 00:09:06.078
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:07.513
Trump...

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:09.148
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:11.050
Trump is clearly nervous
about the impact

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.719
his tariffs are having because
he's backed away from a threat

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:15.654
this week to impose tariffs
on Mexico.

00:09:15.654 --> 00:09:18.157
And to justify that choice,
Trump has been claiming

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:20.592
that there's a secret component
to the Mexico deal

00:09:20.592 --> 00:09:21.860
that he can't talk about.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.829
Yesterday he waved around
a piece of paper

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:26.565
he claimed contained a secret
deal he couldn't show reporters.

00:09:26.565 --> 00:09:28.634
And on Monday
he made a similar claim

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:30.702
during his phone interview
with CNBC.

00:09:30.702 --> 00:09:33.238
-Can you go into exactly
what else was part of that deal

00:09:33.238 --> 00:09:35.507
that you haven't really
outlined yet?

00:09:35.507 --> 00:09:38.411
-Well, I'm gonna tell you
that most people understand

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:39.979
that the people having to do

00:09:39.979 --> 00:09:42.581
with borders
and illegal immigration

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.049
and immigration of any kind,

00:09:44.049 --> 00:09:46.218
they understand
exactly what that is.

00:09:46.218 --> 00:09:48.820
But we purposely said
we wouldn't mention it
for a little while.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:51.323
It's going to be brought up
because it has to be brought

00:09:51.323 --> 00:09:53.592
by their legislative body.

00:09:53.592 --> 00:09:55.727
It's got to be taken to a vote.

00:09:55.727 --> 00:09:57.162
So we didn't bring it up,

00:09:57.162 --> 00:09:59.531
but most people know
that answer, Joe.

00:09:59.531 --> 00:10:01.600
-The nicest thing
you can say about Trump

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:03.869
is that he always makes it
obvious when he's lying.

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:05.804
In fact,
if you're ever wondering

00:10:05.804 --> 00:10:08.807
how insane a Trump answer is,
just imagine it as a response

00:10:08.807 --> 00:10:10.008
on Final Jeopardy!

00:10:10.008 --> 00:10:12.411
The clue was,
"it's the capital of Vermont."

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:13.779
James, you answered
"Montpellier."

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:16.315 line:0%
And, Donald, you answered,
"Well, I'm going to tell you

00:10:16.315 --> 00:10:18.884 line:0%
that most people understand
that the people having to do

00:10:18.884 --> 00:10:21.386 line:0%
with Vermont, they understand
exactly what that is.

00:10:21.386 --> 00:10:23.822 line:0%
But we purposely said
we wouldn't mention it
for a little while.

00:10:23.822 --> 00:10:25.091 line:0%
So we didn't bring it up.

00:10:25.091 --> 00:10:27.726 line:0%
But most people
know that answer, Alex."

00:10:27.726 --> 00:10:28.727 line:0%
[ Buzzer ]

00:10:28.727 --> 00:10:30.730 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:36.635 --> 00:10:38.470
And how much did you wager?

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:41.707
$11 gazillion?!

00:10:41.707 --> 00:10:43.409
Trump is lying
about his poll numbers

00:10:43.409 --> 00:10:44.810
in places like Iowa and Michigan

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.945
because his trade policies
are hurting him there.

00:10:46.945 --> 00:10:49.114
It's early, but when it comes
to Trump's tariffs,

00:10:49.114 --> 00:10:50.849
voters definitely
aren't saying...

00:10:50.849 --> 00:10:52.350
-I like it! I love it!

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:54.620
-This has been "A Closer Look."

